  "results": [
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1",
      "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 0.5,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "wizards' college": "synthesis_gap",
        "arcane lockdown": "hit",
        "wards": "synthesis_gap",
        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a city-wide magical lockdown/purification, but the catch is it affects the entire population and could isolate parts of the city or cause major disruption.\n\nBased on the available facts, the proposal tied to the emergency meeting is a **\u201cplanned magical lockdown\u201d** and possibly a **city-wide purification effect**, as \u201cEntire city is within purification scope\u201d (CANON, the city). This aligns with the council actively \u201cchoosing a plan for handling city citizens in relation to the tainted meat issue\u201d (OBSERVED, the city).\n\nThe catch is significant:\n- It would **impact the entire city population** (\u201cThe plan targets involvement of the entire city population\u201d \u2013 OBSERVED).\n- It risks **isolating sections of the city** if \u201ckey tunnels or access points are sealed\u201d (OBSERVED operational status).\n- The city\u2019s **defenses are already a concern regarding their integrity** (CANON), so a full lockdown could strain or destabilize them further.\n\nThere is no explicit mention of \u201cwizards\u201d making the request in the provided context, but the arcane nature of the plan strongly implies their involvement.  \n\nKey Attributes:\n- Governance: Council voting on crisis response plan (OBSERVED)\n- Defenses: Proposed arcane lockdown; integrity concerns (CANON)\n- Operational Status: Planned magical lockdown; city under threat (OBSERVED)\n- Geography: Entire city affected; risk of isolation via sealed passages (CANON/OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster",
      "question": "Who's actually in the council chamber for the Session 12 fight with the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "thalia",
        "wolf",
        "guards"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
