      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "shepherds": "hit",
        "maelthor": "hit",
        "worship": "retriever_gap",
        "cult": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherds are a cult known as the Shepherd\u2019s Flock, and they serve or are aligned with the power/entity Maelthor.\n\nThe \u201cShepherds\u201d refers to the **Shepherd\u2019s Flock**, a cult group currently active in the city (notably staging a protest at the gates). They recruit individuals\u2014especially those who have been \u201ctransformed\u201d\u2014and indoctrinate them into their mission.\n\nTheir beliefs center on **Maelthor**, whom they follow and justify their actions through. The flock views their actions (including violent or extreme ones) as **necessary sacrifices to cleanse the world of impurities** and advance Maelthor\u2019s influence. They also push an ideology tied to **human supremacy**.\n\nThere\u2019s also a strong propaganda element: outwardly, they frame events as defensive actions against non-human threats, while internally they are organized, recruiting, and coordinated.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Faction: Followers of Maelthor (OBSERVED)\n- Role: Cultists staging a protest (CANON)\n- Goals: Recruitment, \u201ccleansing\u201d the world, advancing Maelthor\u2019s influence, human supremacy (CANON)\n- Operations: Actively recruiting transformed individuals (OBSERVED)\n- Presence: Visible protest movement at city gates (CANON)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_the_city_council_2",
      "question": "Who speaks for the wizards on the council, and what's his angle on the cult?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "semantic_verdict": "pass_updated",
      "must_hits": [
