        "wizard's college": "hit",
        "detect": "hit",
        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards; he sees the cult\u2019s magic as a dangerous perversion and pushes for aggressive arcane detection and containment (including lockdown measures).\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright is the council\u2019s arcane voice (OBSERVED role: \u201cRepresentative of the Arcane,\u201d Head of the Wizard\u2019s College). His stance on the cult is strongly interventionist: he is \u201cdeeply troubled by the dark magic at play\u201d and explicitly \u201cviews corrupted meat as a perversion of magic\u201d (CANON). \n\nPractically, his angle is to bring the full weight of the Wizard\u2019s College to bear\u2014he plans to deploy detection spells and a rune system to identify corruption, and even proposes a magical lockdown of the city (OBSERVED goals). He treats the cult as an urgent, systemic magical threat that must be exposed and contained quickly, rather than handled through slower or purely mundane means.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; council\u2019s arcane representative  \n- Faction: Wizard\u2019s College  \n- Goals: Magical lockdown; detection runes; deploy arcane resources  \n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as a serious magical corruption/perversion  \n- Approach: Proactive, city-wide magical detection and containment",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
