      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states: The Wolf previously **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cattempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d**, even noted as **\u201cescapes.\u201d** However, a later OBSERVED outcome shows Bonogo **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it\u201d** and the Wolf\u2019s condition as **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**  \nBecause decapitation is a terminal outcome, it supersedes the earlier escape attempt. The current, final state is that the Wolf is dead.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Central adversary in the council chamber (CANON)\n- Operational Status: Attempted invisible escape via secret passage (OBSERVED, earlier)\n- Physical Condition: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED, terminal)\n- Relationship: Killed and processed by Bonogo (OBSERVED)\n\nNet: He doesn\u2019t get away\u2014the escape fails, and he\u2019s definitively neutralized.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
