      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no explicit evidence that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; the projection only shows she\u2019s being directed by the Wolf, which suggests a different mechanism (likely influence or manipulation), but it\u2019s not confirmed.\n\nFrom the available facts:\n- **OBSERVED (the Wolf goals):** \u201corders Thalia to attack the group.\u201d  \n- **OBSERVED (Guards physical_condition):** corrupted guards are marked by \u201can oily sheen to their eyes.\u201d  \n- **OBSERVED (the Wolf physical_condition):** also has \u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d tying him to the same corruption effect.\n\nHowever, **there are no facts describing Thalia with an oily sheen, corruption, or physical symptoms**. That absence matters: the guards\u2019 corruption is clearly signposted, while Thalia\u2019s is not.\n\nSo the current best-supported interpretation is:\n- Thalia is **acting under the Wolf\u2019s command**, but\n- It is **not confirmed she shares the same corruption state as the guards**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia: No data on physical condition or corruption state in projection.\n- Guards: Corruption explicitly marked by \u201coily sheen to their eyes.\u201d\n- The Wolf: Also shows \u201coily sheen,\u201d and is issuing commands to Thalia.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2",
