      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room fights back with **arcane traps, illusion effects, and environmental hazards**\u2014especially targeting anyone without amulets\u2014causing paralysis, force damage, disorientation, and falling debris.\n\n**What the room throws at them (CANON + OBSERVED):**\n- **Arcane trap bursts (CANON/OBSERVED)**: These trigger against the Players if they lack amulets, dealing **2d6 force damage** and potentially leaving them **temporarily paralyzed**.\n- **Selective targeting via amulets (CANON)**: Guards are **exempt from arcane trap targeting** because their amulets mark them as friendly; Players may get hammered if they don\u2019t have that protection.\n- **Illusion interference (CANON)**: The room creates **illusory walls/illusion spells**, actively **disorienting** the Players and messing with positioning and line of sight.\n- **Falling debris hazards (OBSERVED)**: The environment itself becomes unstable, forcing Players to **dodge falling debris** mid-fight.\n- **Rune alarm escalation (OBSERVED)**: **Rune alarms** alert defenders, increasing pressure and reinforcing the encounter.\n- **Ambient feedback (CANON)**: The **wall hum changes** as events trigger\u2014subtle, but a cue that the room is reacting dynamically.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps, amulet-based targeting system\n- Environment: Illusions, falling debris, reactive architecture (hum)\n- Security: Rune alarms tied to guard response",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
