      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Inaction accelerates the city toward disaster\u2014coordinated threats advance unchecked, unrest worsens, and drastic measures like a magical lockdown risk isolating parts of the city.\n\nIf the council stalls, several things \u201cbite\u201d you at once:\n\n- **Escalation of the core threat (OBSERVED \u2013 the city):** The city is \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate,\u201d and \u201csomething wrong is happening\u2026 its stability and well-being are threatened by the cult.\u201d Delay directly advances the enemy\u2019s timeline.\n- **Coordinated attacks land (CANON \u2013 geography):** The city already anticipates \u201ccoordinated attacks across the city.\u201d Inaction gives those plans time to synchronize and hit multiple \u0646\u0642\u0627\u0637 at once.\n- **Lockdown consequences (CANON/OBSERVED \u2013 defenses & status):** A \u201cproposed arcane lockdown\u201d could be enacted reactively, risking parts of the city being \u201cisolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed.\u201d\n- **Civil unrest worsens (CANON \u2013 atmosphere):** Existing protest over the \u201cunfair toll\u201d intensifies, straining order and distracting resources.\n- **Economic damage (CANON \u2013 economy):** The festival is crucial; instability or contamination (tainted meat issue) threatens a key revenue driver.\n\n**Key Attributes**\n- Defenses: Weak points; possible arcane lockdown\n- Geography: Hidden passages, sewers; citywide attack vectors\n- Governance: Council deadlock over tainted meat response\n- Operational Status: Imminent disaster pressure; cult threat; risk of isolation\n- Economy: Festival-dependent, vulnerable to disruption\n- Atmosphere: Active unrest over tolls",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_arch_current",
