      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows clear signs of chaos and corruption\u2014The Wolf is dead (\"Decapitated; head removed from body;\"), guards are tense or compromised, and there are strong clues pointing to deception, illusion, and a possible escape route beneath the chamber.\n\nWhat stands out:\n\n- The Wolf\u2019s body is the centerpiece: **\"Decapitated; head removed from body;\"** (OBSERVED). This is a definitive, public end to the confrontation.\n- Several guards show corruption: **\u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), marking them as compromised or influenced.\n- The room still carries the confusion of the fight: The Wolf was using **illusory duplicates** (CANON), so there may be lingering uncertainty about what was real.\n- Guards are **visibly tense and in disbelief** (OBSERVED), suggesting the situation is not fully under control.\n- There are hints of deeper danger: The Wolf had been **attempting to escape through a secret passage beneath the council chamber** (OBSERVED), implying something hidden below.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps may exist (implied by player interaction context, CANON).\n- Demographics: ~8 guards, some corrupted (OBSERVED).\n- Geography: Secret passage beneath the chamber (OBSERVED).\n- Operational Status: Scene of a recent battle; instability and infiltration evident (OBSERVED).",
      "embedding_similarity": null
