      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Chamber was heavily disrupted\u2014magical defenses activated, illusions and a Fireball reshaped the space, and it ended up disheveled, with the Wolf\u2019s **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d** marking a major outcome.\n\nDuring Session 12 (OBSERVED):\n- The room was **almost entirely lit up by Fireball**, dramatically altering visibility and likely scorching or damaging surfaces.\n- **Runes along the walls activated** in response to spellcasting (Caelynn), meaning dormant defenses became active mid-encounter.\n- **Illusory walls** were present and influencing movement and perception, changing how the space functioned tactically.\n- The chamber ended in a **Disheveled** physical state, indicating general destruction or disorder from the fight.\n- The **hidden trapdoor** is part of the room\u2019s geography; combined with the Wolf\u2019s escape attempt, it may have become tactically relevant, though no explicit change is recorded.\n\nAdditionally, the confrontation culminated in the Wolf being **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d**, a major in-room event with lasting narrative impact.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Atmosphere: Fireball illumination; tense, battle-altered\n- Defenses: Activated runes; illusory walls; magical wards engaged\n- Geography: Circular chamber; central table; hidden trapdoor\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled",
