      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events and trying to escape; after, he\u2019s a broken, corrupted figure who ends in **\"Decapitated; head removed from body;\"** with signs of deeper influence.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **second-in-command guard** and **cult-aligned saboteur** working inside the council.\n- He actively **deceives and manipulates** (steering discussions, downplaying threats).\n- Uses **illusory duplicates** and **Invisibility** to confuse and evade.\n- Operationally focused on **escape via secret tunnel** and avoiding capture.\n- Mentally: alert, calculating, but already sensing danger.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state shifts to **desperate and regretful**, even **begging to be killed**.\n- Physical corruption is \u0938\u094d\u092a\u0937\u094d\u091f: **\u201coily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**\n- He is no longer an active agent\u2014his arc ends with **\"Decapitated; head removed from body;\"**\n- This confirms both **defeat** and the likely **depth of cult corruption/control**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur \u2192 defeated target\n- Mental State: Calculated deception \u2192 desperation, regret\n- Physical Condition: Illusions/invisibility \u2192 corrupted (oily eyes) \u2192 **\"Decapitated; head removed from body;\"**\n- Tactics: Manipulation and escape \u2192 none (neutralized)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
