        "not corrupted": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted**\u2014she was **ensorcelled and manipulated by the Wolf**, who used that influence to control her actions and obscure the truth.\n\nThalia\u2019s state is consistently described as **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** and **\u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d** (OBSERVED). Crucially, **\u201cThalia does not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d**, which is a clear marker of corruption seen in others (like guards and the Wolf). Her mental state includes **\u201cInnocent\u201d** and that her **\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d**, after which she **\u201crealizes how dire the situation truly is\u201d**\u2014indicating regained autonomy.\n\nBy contrast, the Wolf is explicitly tied to corruption: **\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes\u201d** and acts as a **\u201ccorrupting_influence\u201d** (CANON/OBSERVED). He also **orders Thalia to attack the group**, showing direct control.\n\nSo the relationship is:\n- The Wolf = corrupted agent and manipulator  \n- Thalia = controlled pawn, not inherently corrupted  \n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia physical_condition: \u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d; no oily sheen  \n- Thalia mental_state: \u201cInnocent\u201d; \u201cCharmed status ended\u201d  \n- Thalia loyalty: serves the Wolf (under influence), protector of the city  \n- Wolf physical_condition: \u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d  \n- Wolf role: cultist, saboteur, corrupting influence",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
